  "zm_subcloud_tendency": {
   "description": "Subcloud tendency of q1q2_pjr, (1/dsubcld)(-F[k]) with F = zm_flux the layer-centered plume flux (zm_convr.F90:2612-2619): the negative of the plume flux at level k divided by the subcloud layer thickness dsubcld, gathered at index maxg by the tendency masks. Applied once for moisture (sub_dqdt, xu = qu, xd = qd, xhat = qhat) and once for dry static energy (sub_dsdt, xu = su, xd = sd, xhat = shat).",
   "params": [
    "mu",
    "xu",
    "md",
    "xd",
    "xhat",
    "dsubcld"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "faq",
    "output_idx": [
     "k"
    ],
    "args": [
     "mu",
     "xu",
     "md",
     "xd",
     "xhat"
    ],
    "ranges": {
     "k": {
      "from": "lev"
     }
    },
    "expr": {
     "op": "*",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": "/",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "const",
         "args": [],
         "value": 1.0,
         "units": "1"
        },
        "dsubcld"
       ]
      },
      {
       "op": "*",
       "args": [
        {
         "op": "const",
         "args": [],
         "value": -1.0,
         "units": "1"
        },
        {
         "op": "apply_expression_template",
         "args": [],
         "name": "zm_flux",
         "bindings": {
          "mu": {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "mu",
            "k"
           ]
          },
          "xu": {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "xu",
            "k"
           ]
          },
          "md": {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "md",
            "k"
           ]
          },
          "xd": {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "xd",
            "k"
           ]
          },
          "xhat": {
           "op": "index",
           "args": [
            "xhat",
            "k"
           ]
          }
         }
        }
       ]
      }
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "estbl_tmax": {
   "description": "The upper clamp of the estbl saturation-vapor-pressure lookup: tmax = 375.16 K (wv_saturation.F90:96, the public module parameter; estblf clamps T to it at wv_saturation.F90:388, so the 251st table knot at 377.16 K is unreachable). Zero-parameter constant-fragment template applied with empty bindings.",
   "params": [],
   "body": {
    "op": "const",
    "args": [],
    "value": 375.16,
    "units": "K"
   }
  },
  "estbl_es0": {
   "description": "The saturation vapor pressure of the estbl table lookup, es0 = estbl[min(T, tmax)]: the linear interpolation of the estbl function table on the clamped temperature min(T, tmax), with estbl_tmax the wv_saturation.F90:96 clamp (estblf of wv_saturation.F90:388) and the table's own flat out-of-bounds clamps. The table itself must be declared by the CONSUMING document's function_tables block (the CLI resolves table_lookup only against the declaring document - importing the table from a library or a mounted subsystem fails with [table_lookup_unknown_table], see README-cam-zm-evap.md), so cam_wv_saturation.esm and cam_zm_evap.esm each carry the identical data copy and both call this single law: WvSaturation binds T to its T, ZMevap to its layer temperature t1; the saturation mixing ratio is then svp_to_qsat(es0, p) in both callers.",
   "params": [
    "T"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "table_lookup",
    "table": "estbl",
    "axes": {
     "T": {
      "op": "min",
      "args": [
       "T",
       {
        "op": "apply_expression_template",
        "args": [],
        "name": "estbl_tmax",
        "bindings": {}
       }
      ]
     }
    },
    "args": []
   }
  },
  "guarded_ratio": {
   "description": "Guarded ratio of the RRTMG shortwave cloud-optics conversion (radsw.F90:437-475): ratio = x/y when y > 0, else fallback. The three solver-input ratios share the one branch structure: ssa = tau_w/tau with fallback 1 (tau = 0 -> ssa = 1), asm = tau_w_g/tau_w and fsfc = tau_w_f/tau_w with fallback 0 (tau_w = 0 -> 0). The Fortran guards the denominator with max(y, 1e-80) instead of branching, but the two are identical whenever y <= 0 selects the fallback (x/max(y,1e-80) is never evaluated in the else branch) and the max is vacuous for y > 0 (every dump ratio y > 1e-80; the stage-1 validator verifies ssa = tau_w/tau, asm = tau_w_g/tau_w, fsfc = tau_w_f/tau_w to rel 1e-12 where the denominators are positive).",
   "params": [
    "x",
    "y",
    "fallback"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "ifelse",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": ">",
      "args": [
       "y",
       {
        "op": "const",
        "args": [],
        "value": 0.0,
        "units": "1"
       }
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "/",
      "args": [
       "x",
       "y"
      ]
     },
     "fallback"
    ]
   }
  },
  "edge_shift": {
   "description": "The shared-edge law of the RRTMG state construction (rrtmg_state.F90:141-144, 110-120): the upper interface of RRTMG layer k is the lower interface of layer k+1, so hi(k) = lo(k+1) for k = 1..n-1 and hi(n) = the surface boundary value sfc, written as a per-k gather over the index set kset. Used for the pressure edges (pint_hi from pint_lo, with the surface pressure r_state%pintmb(num_rrtmg_levs+1) = pstate%pint(pverp), F90:158-159) and the temperature edges (T_ifc_hi from T_ifc_lo, with the surface interface temperature tint(pverp) from the surface upwelling flux, F90:110-120).",
   "params": [
    "lo",
    "sfc",
    "n",
    "kset"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "faq",
    "output_idx": [
     "kk"
    ],
    "args": [],
    "ranges": {
     "kk": {
      "from": "kset"
     }
    },
    "expr": {
     "op": "ifelse",
     "args": [
      {
       "op": "<=",
       "args": [
        "kk",
        "n"
       ]
      },
      {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "lo",
        {
         "op": "+",
         "args": [
          "kk",
          1
         ]
        }
       ]
      },
      "sfc"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "band_gather": {
   "description": "Gather of a per-band (band x lev) optics field to the McICA g-point axis: out[g, k] = x[band_of[g], k] over the g-point and level index sets named by the gset/lset template parameters (the SW and LW models bind them to their own gpt axes, ngptsw = 112 and ngptlw = 140). band_of is the fixed RRTMG k-distribution band->g-point map (rrtmg_sw_init.f90:266-280, counts 6,12,8,8,10,10,2,10,8,6,6,8,6,12; rrtmg_lw_init.f90:308, counts 10,12,16,14,16,8,12,8,12,6,8,8,4,2,2,2), declared as a [gpt]-shaped parameter in the consuming models.",
   "params": [
    "x",
    "band_of",
    "gset",
    "lset"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "faq",
    "output_idx": [
     "g",
     "k"
    ],
    "args": [],
    "ranges": {
     "g": {
      "from": "gset"
     },
     "k": {
      "from": "lset"
     }
    },
    "expr": {
     "op": "index",
     "args": [
      "x",
      {
       "op": "index",
       "args": [
        "band_of",
        "g"
       ]
      },
      "k"
     ]
    }
   }
  },
  "mcica_subcolumn": {
   "description": "The McICA subcolumn cloud-optics masking (mcica_subcol_gen_sw.f90:439-444, mcica_subcol_gen_lw.f90:408-416): where the stochastic subcolumn is cloudy (cld_sto = 1) the subcolumn optics equal the in-cloud band value x, where clear (cld_sto = 0) they equal the fill value: out = cld_sto*x + (1 - cld_sto)*fill. The solver boundary fills tauc_sto/asmc_sto/fsfc_sto with 0 and ssac_sto with 1 (the clear-sky single-scattering albedo). cld_sto is the RNG output of the deterministic McICA generator (permuteseed 1 SW / 150 LW, single column) and is an input to the consuming models.",
   "params": [
    "x",
    "cld_sto",
    "fill"
   ],
   "body": {
    "op": "+",
    "args": [
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       "cld_sto",
       "x"
      ]
     },
     {
      "op": "*",
      "args": [
       {
        "op": "-",
        "args": [
         {
          "op": "const",
          "args": [],
          "value": 1.0,
          "units": "1"
         },
         "cld_sto"
        ]
       },
       "fill"
      ]
     }
    ]
   }
  }
 }
}